) control block must be passed in with each call for the private use of the head.  cb should be a pointer to a block of EtherNetFace.controlBlockSize words.  It must be allocated within the first 64K and must be quad word aligned.  The data buffer must be quad word aligned and less than 32K words long.  When GetStatus[cb] returns anything other than pending, both the control block and the data buffer are available for reuse. l4283d3633\i141I2i35I29i9b145B7I13i29I7i70I l4283d3633\i1IGetStatus: PROCEDURE [cb: ControlBlock] RETURNS [status: Status];l3648d2998e6\b10B1f1 9f0 20f1 7f0-- Returns the status of the packet associated with this control block.  See the comments on Status below. l4283d3633\i93I6i9IGetRetries: PROCEDURE [cb: ControlBlock] RETURNS [CARDINAL];l3648d2998e6\b11B1f1 9f0 20f1 7f0 2f1 8f0-- Returns the number of times the packet was retransmitted because of collisions.l4283d3633\i82IGetPacketLength: PROCEDURE [cb: ControlBlock] RETURNS [CARDINAL];l3648d2998e6\b16B1f1 9f0 20f1 7f0 2f1 8f0-- Returns the length in words of a recently arrived packet.l4283d3633\i60IGetPacketsMissed: PROCEDURE [DeviceHandle] RETURNS [CARDINAL];l3648d2998e6\b17B1f1 9f0 1f1 22f0 2f1 8f0-- Returns the number of input packets missed because a buffer was not ready.l4283d3633\i77I-- TYPESe12\iDeviceHandle: TYPE[1];l3351d2998e6\14f1 4f0GlobalStatePtr: TYPE = Environment.Base RELATIVE POINTER;l3351d2998e6\16f1 4f0 3f1 12f0 5f1 16f0Status: TYPE = {pending, ok,  overrun,  -- Input data arrived when FIFO was full  underrun,  -- Output FIFO went empty before end of packet was set  packetTooLong,  -- Input packet didn't fit into buffer  tooManyCollisions,  -- More than 16 attempts to transmit the same packet  crc,  crcAndBadAlignment,  badAlignmentButOkCrc,  otherError};e12\8f1 4f0-- Note: The error conditions are an open ended set to allow a smart driver to collect statistics.  Thus new error conditions may be added to allow more sophisticated data collection, so a driver should not get upset if it encounters a strange error status that it does not understand.  Dumb drivers should only check for pending or ok and consider everything else as an error.l4283d3633\i322I7i4I2iControlBlock: TYPE = LONG POINTER TO ControlBlockRecord;e12\14f1 4f0 3f1 16f0ControlBlockRecord: TYPE;\20f1 4f0-- EXPORTED VARIABLESe12\iglobalStateSize: READONLY CARDINAL;l3351d2998e6\b16B1f1 17f0controlBlockSize: READONLY CARDINAL;l3351d2998\b18f1B17f0 1bnullDeviceHandle: READONLY DeviceHandle;l3351d2998\b17B1f1 8f0 14bhearSelf: READONLY BOOLEAN;l3351d2998\b9B1f1 16f0 1b-- CONSTANTSe12\iEND.e6\f1 3f0LOGl4269d2999e36(635)\iTime: February 4, 1980  5:48 PM	By: McJones	Action: Create filel4269d2999e6\i63ITime: February 6, 1980  12:54 PM	By: Dawson	Action: Add interface itemsl4269d2999\i71ITime: April 18, 1980  5:51 PM	By: Murray	Action: Giant Cleanupl4269d2999\i62ITime: August 20, 1980  2:05 PM	By: BLyon	Action: renames EthernetFace to EthernetOneFace and added hearSelfl4269d2999\iTime: September 5, 1980  12:11 AM	By: HGM	Action: fix typos, add ControlBlockRecordl4269d2999\i65I18i